1
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:04,250
Lesson 15.

2
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,610
Nicole practices her election speech.

3
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:11,070
Nicole is running for student body president.

4
00:00:11,619 --> 00:00:13,429
She must give a speech next week.

5
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:16,189
She discusses this speech with her mother.

6
00:00:17,539 --> 00:00:18,549
What's up, Nicole?

7
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:22,250
I pulled an all-nighter working on my election speech.

8
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:24,750
No wonder you look like a basket case.

9
00:00:25,239 --> 00:00:26,549
Did you finish your speech?

10
00:00:26,839 --> 00:00:27,269
Yes.

11
00:00:27,579 --> 00:00:28,709
At 6 a.m.

12
00:00:29,299 --> 00:00:31,469
That must be a load off your mind.

13
00:00:31,839 --> 00:00:32,490
It's not.

14
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,030
I've got to give the speech tomorrow in front of 1,500 people.

15
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:38,789
I'm a nervous wreck.

16
00:00:39,719 --> 00:00:41,670
Just remember the old rule of thumb.

17
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,689
Imagine your audience naked.

18
00:00:44,619 --> 00:00:45,689
That's gross.

19
00:00:46,079 --> 00:00:47,350
Why would I want to do that?

20
00:00:47,939 --> 00:00:51,229
According to conventional wisdom, it'll make you less nervous.

21
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,990
Only practice will do the trick.

22
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:56,490
Okay, let's hear the speech.

23
00:00:57,039 --> 00:00:58,949
Good afternoon, everyone.

24
00:00:59,399 --> 00:01:01,689
There are four candidates running for president.

25
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:03,949
You think you have several choices.

26
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:07,010
In reality, you have just one choice.

27
00:01:07,459 --> 00:01:07,750
Me?

28
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:09,950
You can't say that.

29
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:12,109
You'll turn off your audience immediately.

30
00:01:12,799 --> 00:01:14,490
It sounds like I have a big head.

31
00:01:15,060 --> 00:01:15,770
I'll say.

